When I do a FC using Windows XP I get that the two "Sea Devil" files differ by only two consecutive bytes (not three bytes).  The differences are:

Sea Devil                 $2282: $36 $12

Sea Devil (Homemade Cart) $2282: $87 $2F

It will take a little but of work so see what these bytes are.  In the cartridges made by Bally, the graphics are typically at the end of the cart (but not always).  Of course, graphics can be put ANYWHERE, so that doesn't tell us anything other than a guess.  Also, looking at the homemade cart it's POSSIBLE that $2F87 is an address towards the end of memory on the homemade cart, but it requires more investigation to figure that out.

I plan to take a look at the cart using MESS.  I can use the MESS Debugger to determine when the console is reading from $2282 or $2283.  Once I figure that out, I can work backward to see what is going on.  I'm not sure if I'll have time to get to it today-- but I did want to take an initial look at both the files just to get an idea.

Adam

